\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Disposer Supreme, and Judge of the earth
\par Who choosest for Thine the weak and the poor;
\par To frail earthen vessels and things of no worth
\par Entrusting Thy riches, which aye shall endure:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Those vessels soon fail, though full of Thy light,
\par And at Thy decree are broken and gone;
\par Then brightly appeareth Thy truth in its might,
\par As through the clouds riven the lightnings have shone.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Like clouds are they borne to do Thy great will,
\par And swift as the winds about the world go;
\par The word with His wisdom their spirits doth fill,
\par They thunder, they lighten, the waters o'erflow.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Their sound goeth forth: Christ Jesus is Lord!
\par Then Satan doth fear, his citadels fall:
\par As when the dread trumpets went forth at Thy word,
\par And one long blast shattered the Canaanite's wall.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Then loud be their trump, and stirring their sound,
\par To rouse us, O Lord, from slumber of sin;
\par The lights Thou hast kindled in darkness around,
\par O may they illumine our spirits within!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. All honour and praise, dominion and might,
\par To God Three in one eternally be;
\par Who round us hath shed His marvellous light,
\par And called u from darkness His glory to see!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

